WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.258 --> 00:00:02.980
(light cheerful music)

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.010
- [Narrator] The service dogs in training from Doggy Do Good

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.850
have a big day ahead of them.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:08.633
It's beach day!

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.520
The sun, the surf, and boundless distractions

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.170
that could cause any of these dogs to flunk

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.470
out of Service Dog School.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.593
This is Puppy Prep.

00:00:19.784 --> 00:00:23.117
^(light cheerful music)

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.320
None of the pups are more excited to smell that ocean air

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.600
^than eight-month-old Golden Retriever, Luke.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.610
He's been hanging out by the beach since

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.210
he was only a couple months old.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:06.223
^His half-sister, Remmy, is also excited,

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.403
maybe too excited.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.180
It's all right for her to take a second

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.180
and adjust to the new sights and smells,

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.830
but when it comes time for work,

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.420
Remmy's going to need to focus.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.230
For these puppies, the first order of business

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:24.053
at any new location is to sample the local grass.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.320
While they're not supposed to chew on the foliage,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.940
it's easy for the pups to sneak a bite

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.913
when the trainers have their backs turned.

00:01:31.201 --> 00:01:33.401
And the trainers turn their back frequently.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:35.870
Having this many puppies around draws attention,

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:38.593
and people are excited to learn about the service dogs.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.043
But Nelly and Remmy are taking this chance to mess around.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.070
(dogs barking)

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.370
The dogs aren't supposed to go on the sand after 10:00,

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.960
and while special exception can be made for service animals,

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.610
there's no shortage of other activities by the ocean,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:53.883
like the playground.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:57.190
The playground offers a multitude of different surfaces,

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:58.873
sounds, and experiences.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.973
All of this builds confidence,

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.010
getting the puppies ready for anything.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.023
^First one up, six-month-old Chocolate Lab, Benelli.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.513
Climbing on rocks and walking on sand may appear simple,

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.470
but it's actually building the puppy's comfort

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.013
on a variety of surfaces.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:18.200
Wherever Benelli goes, she needs to be focused

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:21.150
not on where she's standing but on what her owner may need.

00:02:21.625 --> 00:02:22.570
- Good girl.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:24.570
- [Narrator] After breezing through the different surfaces,

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.740
it's time for something that will really disorient her.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:27.573
- Good girl.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.110
- [Narrator] The slide.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.450
While Benelli's future owners may never actually

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.490
take her down a slide, it's important she has confidence

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.713
to handle all kinds of new experiences.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:42.520
At first, she's nervous, but with some coaxing

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.100
and the promise of treat...

00:02:45.009 --> 00:02:45.842
- Good girl!

00:02:45.842 --> 00:02:46.675
- [Narrator] ...even a puppy like Benelli

00:02:46.675 --> 00:02:47.508
can find her courage.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.623
Now back on firm land,

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.700
the trainer is sure to praise Benelli up,

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.320
building a connection in the puppy's mind

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.463
between bravery and reward.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.850
Fresh off the excitement of the slide,

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.050
Trainer Paul tosses his keys to ensure Benelli

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.307
still knows it's work time.

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:03.440
- Good, get it.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:04.739
- [Narrator] And she happily does her job.

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:06.822
- Benelli, great, get it.

00:03:07.463 --> 00:03:08.296
Benelli, get it.

00:03:08.296 --> 00:03:09.129
Good girl.

00:03:09.129 --> 00:03:10.090
- [Narrator] There's still one more slide for

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.163
Benelli to attempt.

00:03:11.348 --> 00:03:13.320
(dramatic drumbeats)

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.543
The spiral slide.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.163
That is, if she can get up to it.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.938
With a bit of a running start...

00:03:20.938 --> 00:03:21.771
- Benelli, jump.

00:03:21.771 --> 00:03:22.604
- [Narrator] ...she makes the leap.

00:03:22.604 --> 00:03:23.437
- Good girl.

00:03:23.437 --> 00:03:24.480
- [Narrator] Her lesson from the other slide

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.080
has her excited to try this one.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.740
Having never seen them before five minutes ago,

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.640
slides are now simple for the six-month-old Chocolate Lab.

00:03:33.096 --> 00:03:34.263
- Woo hoo hoo!

00:03:35.094 --> 00:03:36.761
Good girl!
Good girl.

00:03:38.656 --> 00:03:40.906
- [Narrator] Back with the dogs in down stay,

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.693
^Karen tries to refocus Remmy.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.270
She tries to get the Golden to heel,

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.153
and focus in,

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.860
but the eight-month-old won't settle down.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:50.773
This isn't good.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.320
Remmy's future owner will count on her,

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:54.733
day in and day out.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.590
And, it looks like Remmy's lack of focus

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.033
is starting to spread.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.320
Luke, get back!

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.420
Come on, Karen's trying to focus on Remmy.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.460
Kaya, are you serious?

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:07.293
Come on!

00:04:07.293 --> 00:04:08.126
- Kaya, no!

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.140
- [Narrator] All three Goldens have the sillies now,

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.713
even usually dependable Luke.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.033
Kaya has to refocus, and quick.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.100
It's her turn to walk the playground.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.315
^The eight-month-old enjoys jumping on different surfaces.

00:04:22.315 --> 00:04:23.315
- Good girl!

00:04:23.973 --> 00:04:24.806
Good girl.

00:04:25.958 --> 00:04:26.820
Come on, let's go.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.653
- [Narrator] The straight slide.

00:04:27.653 --> 00:04:28.941
- Good girl!

00:04:28.941 --> 00:04:30.442
Good girl, Kaya!

00:04:30.442 --> 00:04:31.275
Good girl!

00:04:31.275 --> 00:04:33.060
- [Narrator] And when it's time for the spiral slide,

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.350
what was a tough jump for Benelli

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.813
is an easy hop for Kaya.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.993
But, what goes up must come down,

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.620
and Kaya's confused how that's supposed to happen.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:48.113
When Sandy, the owner of Doggie Do Good, leads the way,

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.163
Kaya eventually figures it out.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.193
She's immediately praised for her bravery.

00:04:53.193 --> 00:04:54.190
- Good girl!

00:04:55.151 --> 00:04:55.984
Good girl!

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.470
- [Narrator] A second attempt down the slide...

00:05:01.639 --> 00:05:03.722
(laughs)

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:05.967
Oh, look at you.

00:05:06.048 --> 00:05:06.881
Oh, no.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.806
Good try, Kaya.
Good try.

00:05:08.806 --> 00:05:09.806
- Good girl.

00:05:09.823 --> 00:05:10.656
Good girl, Kaya.

00:05:10.656 --> 00:05:11.510
- [Narrator] But, what's important

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.183
is that Kaya's conquered her fear, and admirably so.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:17.580
Back in the down stay,

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:19.188
it looks like Remy has finally calmed...

00:05:19.188 --> 00:05:20.021
Oh.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.403
Relax, Remmy.
It's just a bird.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.473
All right.
Good girl, Remmy.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:26.940
Thank goodness you're finally starting

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.840
to show some self-control, otherwise today

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.740
could have been the day you failed at...

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.163
Oh no.

00:05:32.719 --> 00:05:33.552
- [Trainer] Remmy!

00:05:33.552 --> 00:05:34.385
- [Narrator] Breaking from a down stay

00:05:34.385 --> 00:05:36.113
to this degree is a bad sign.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.873
With Karen working with Kaya,

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:41.780
Paul has to leave the dogs to find where Remmy ran off.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.730
Even though they're unsupervised,

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.083
they don't dare to break;

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:48.233
no one wants the fate that's about to befall Remmy.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:49.883
Lockdown.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.130
Remmy now has to think about what she's done,

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.903
and hope it doesn't mean expulsion.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:00.220
^Now, it's Luke's turn to take a lap around the playground.

00:06:01.358 --> 00:06:02.191
- Good boy.

00:06:02.191 --> 00:06:04.660
- [Narrator] His first challenge is the rocking horse.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.830
Karen is trying to get Luke to jump over it,

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:10.253
in preparation for future awkward spaces.

00:06:11.038 --> 00:06:11.871
- Stay.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:12.867
- [Narrator] Luke is not having it.

00:06:12.867 --> 00:06:14.520
- Good boy.
Jump over it.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.740
- [Narrator] He hasn't had problems of bravery in the past,

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:17.933
so this is a new issue.

00:06:17.988 --> 00:06:19.768
- Over it.
Nope.

00:06:19.768 --> 00:06:21.935
Over it.
Good boy, come on.

00:06:22.322 --> 00:06:23.538
- [Narrator] Eventually, our hero figures it out.

00:06:23.538 --> 00:06:24.552
- Good, good!

00:06:24.552 --> 00:06:25.385
Good boy!

00:06:25.403 --> 00:06:26.539
- [Narrator] And Karen is sure to reward his courage.

00:06:26.539 --> 00:06:27.456
- Good job!

00:06:27.749 --> 00:06:29.332
Good boy, let's go!

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.360
- [Narrator] If Luke shows the same hesitation on the slide,

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.193
then...

00:06:34.279 --> 00:06:35.112
- Good boy!

00:06:35.112 --> 00:06:35.945
- [Narrator] ...well, nevermind.

00:06:36.086 --> 00:06:36.919
- Good job, Luke!

00:06:36.919 --> 00:06:37.752
Good boy!

00:06:37.752 --> 00:06:39.340
- [Narrator] Looks like after only a couple attempts,

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:40.220
he's already a pro.

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:41.610
- Good job!
Good boy!

00:06:42.082 --> 00:06:43.053
- [Narrator] Good job, buddy.

00:06:43.053 --> 00:06:43.970
- Good job.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.370
- [Narrator] When Luke returns to down stay,

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.020
he finds Deacon is still getting used to his harness.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.800
He's not quite sure why he can't flip

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.250
all the way over on his back.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:57.020
Paul straightens him out, and it's back to down stay.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:00.393
^Okay, Remmy.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:01.930
^You've had a tough day so far,

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:04.180
so time to redeem yourself on the playground.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:07.213
First up is the rocking horse that Luke struggled with.

00:07:07.351 --> 00:07:08.503
- Come on.
Good girl.

00:07:08.679 --> 00:07:09.512
Over it.

00:07:09.512 --> 00:07:10.650
- [Narrator] Just like with her half-brother,

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.050
it's a matter of confidence.

00:07:14.175 --> 00:07:15.092
- Let's go.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:16.673
- [Narrator] And it suddenly looks

00:07:16.673 --> 00:07:18.410
like Remmy's lost most of hers.

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:19.803
The culprit?

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:22.080
The pirate ship steering wheel.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.492
- Just need a second.

00:07:24.492 --> 00:07:26.550
- [Narrator] Notice how her tail is tucked between her legs?

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.653
So do the trainers.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.680
They're hyper-aware of the pup's attitude,

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:31.853
and this is a huge signal from Remmy.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:34.380
Karen gets down on Remmy's level

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.880
and starts feeding her treats.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.420
She pets her and praises her,

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.020
trying to show Remmy she's safe.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.620
Remmy then has to pass by the wheel several more times,

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:44.670
ensuring the dog has confronted her fear.

00:07:45.613 --> 00:07:46.446
- [Karen] Good girl.

00:07:46.446 --> 00:07:47.360
- [Narrator] If Karen can get Remmy to sniff the wheel

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.690
or be still next to it, that's going to be a great

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:51.690
indication that Remmy's making progress.

00:07:52.928 --> 00:07:53.761
- Good girl!

00:07:53.761 --> 00:07:54.594
- [Narrator] Eventually, a sniff.

00:07:54.594 --> 00:07:55.753
- [Karen] Good job!

00:07:55.807 --> 00:07:57.200
- [Narrator] And after a few more laps,

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.650
her tail starts to wag again.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:02.560
Remmy's done extremely well, and with so much excitement

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.030
already had on the playground,

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:05.780
the slide can wait for another day.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:12.860
^Back on the grass, the undeniable Mr. Pip

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:14.860
^finds himself in an embarrassing situation.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:15.860
- [Trainer] Mr. Pip.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.400
- [Narrator] Because he is by far the worst at down stay,

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:21.853
Mr. Pip has to be tied up, to the other dogs.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:25.723
Luke seems confused why he has to babysit,

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:27.273
but he doesn't mind.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.590
It gives him something to watch

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:29.923
as he snacks on the grass.

00:08:31.233 --> 00:08:32.125
- [Trainer] Luke, leave it.

00:08:32.125 --> 00:08:32.958
Luke, release.

00:08:32.958 --> 00:08:34.690
- [Narrator] Finally, some respect.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.383
Unbelievable.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:40.543
Chin up, Mr. Pip.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:42.853
You're still a hero in our hearts.

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:45.850
(Mr. Pip whines)

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:50.253
^Another hero from Doggie Do Good is recent graduate Sammy.

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:53.850
Sammy transitioned to his forever family

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:57.130
only five months ago, but his bond with handler Bryce

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:58.163
has been immediate.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.723
Sammy helps Bryce with several diagnoses,

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:05.063
including generalized anxiety disorder, ADHD,

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:08.023
inflammatory bowel disease, and bipolar disorder.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:10.360
One way Sammy aids Bryce

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.403
is during Bryce's regular blood draws.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.950
Before going into an appointment,

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.283
Sammy gives Bryce hugs and pressure,

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:18.450
helping to prepare the boy

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.253
for the anxiety the needles cause.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.970
During the draws, Sammy gives Bryce constant pressure

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:25.670
to help him feel more comfortable.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:28.853
Sammy knows Bryce isn't in distress now,

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:31.683
but the 18-month-old lab checks in constantly,

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:34.573
making sure, if Bryce ever needs him, he's there.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.440
While Bryce's family had always had animals,

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.510
at first, they weren't sure about adding a service dog.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.460
The support that Sammy's provided

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.360
in only his first few months, however,

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.703
has made it all worth it.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.430
Someday, the puppies in training

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.370
will have similar bonds with their owners

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.253
and be just as important to a family as Sammy is.

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:01.320
Back with the student pups, it's time

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:02.773
for a long walk on the beach.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:04.610
^Or at least next to it.

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.070
^Remmy's had a big day, so trainer Paul

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:09.003
takes this walk very slow.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:12.060
Whenever Remmy begins to pull away

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:13.710
or move in a different direction,

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:14.823
the trainer stops.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:17.093
This teaches Remmy to stay focused.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:20.470
During a heel, the puppies need to be

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:22.643
paying attention to the handler constantly,

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:24.590
not drifting away on their own line.

00:10:24.972 --> 00:10:25.805
- [Paul] Good girl.

00:10:25.805 --> 00:10:28.013
- [Narrator] Eventually, Remmy starts to do better.

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:32.453
On the stairs, heel is even more difficult for these pups.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.083
Dogs want to be on even ground,

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.163
and prefer bolting up and down steps.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.840
The people they'll someday aid, however,

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.190
may need help with stairs,

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:43.440
so it's important the puppies learn patience.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.200
To end her day, Paul works with Remmy

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:51.513
on one of her special abilities: hug.

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:56.080
As difficult as the day has been for the young Golden,

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:57.640
it's important to remember that someday

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.943
she'll be a huge comfort to a lucky family.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:02.910
It's going to take work and patience,

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:04.960
but it's clear it'll be worth it.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:06.183
- Release.

00:11:07.123 --> 00:11:07.956
Good.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.160
- [Narrator] Some dogs can become nervous on the pier,

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:17.230
as the spaces between the uneven surfaces

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.203
can be uncomfortable under their paws.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.453
^Not our Mr. Pip, though.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:23.290
^He even finds the time to get in

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.563
some of his best down stay work to date.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:28.113
Good boy, Mr. Pip.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:31.710
As the day winds down, Paul begins

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:34.723
^to test a special skill with Kaya: steady.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.710
Steady allows people with mobility issues

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.790
to put pressure on a dog, to sit down,

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.853
stand up, or just regain their balance.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:44.010
It's one of Deacon's specialties,

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:45.853
and might someday be Kaya's as well.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:49.030
Knowing her eight-month-old joints are still developing,

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:51.773
Paul puts only the lightest of pressure over her legs.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:55.640
Once she's grown, she'll be able to take much more weight,

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:57.640
and may even wear a harness like Deacon.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.600
At the end of the day, some dogs took steps forward,

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:07.923
while others, steps back.

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:11.400
For all these puppies, though,

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:13.913
it's still too soon to tell who will flunk out,

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:16.493
and who will graduate Puppy Prep.

00:12:17.173 --> 00:12:20.423
(light cheerful music)

